# Responsive layout & text fit

On every UI change: no overflow/clip; chrome stays one line.

1. Scale via `useResponsive()` / scaled primitives — not hard-coded chrome `fontSize`/padding.
2. Chrome (`AppText` + `fit`): tabs, buttons, field labels, section titles, chips — shrink, don’t wrap.
3. Controls: scaled `minHeight`/padding; tap targets ≥ 44pt.
4. Horizontal text rows: `flexShrink: 1`, `minWidth: 0`.

```tsx
const { spacing, s } = useResponsive();
<AppText variant="callout" fit>{label}</AppText>
```

Body copy may wrap. Prefer `AppText` over raw `Text` for chrome.
